IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Limited -- Hospital Income Policy`

-- Faithful encoding of the fixture contract (fixtures/chubb-policy.txt).
-- This file defines ONLY rules: the shape of a claim (`Claim`) and the
-- predicates needed to decide whether a given claim is covered. No claim
-- data is defined here -- see apply.l4 for the nine benchmark claims.
--
-- Per the encoding brief:
--   * the agreement is assumed signed (Sec.1.1(1)) and the premium is
--     assumed paid on time (Sec.1.1(2), Sec.4.5), so no Claim field
--     represents either fact;
--   * every date/time in a Claim other than the claimant's age is
--     expressed as a NUMBER of months relative to the policy's effective
--     date, never as an absolute calendar date, and no two such relative
--     times are ever compared against each other.

§§ `The shape of a claim`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- Sec.2.1 -- what kind of event caused the hospitalization
    `hospitalization caused by sickness`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization caused by accidental injury`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury was self-inflicted`                               IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Sec.3.1 -- the five general exclusions
    `hospitalization arose out of skydiving`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization arose out of service in the military`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization arose out of service as a fire fighter`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalization arose out of service in the police`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at hospitalization`                                  IS A NUMBER

    -- Sec.1.3 (wellness-visit condition) and Sec.4.6 (one-year term),
    -- both measured in months relative to the policy's effective date
    `months from effective date to hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
    `months from effective date to wellness visit confirmation`         IS A NUMBER

    -- Sec.1.2 -- the other trigger for deemed cancellation
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`      IS A BOOLEAN


§ `Policy in effect and conditions (Sec.1)`

§§ `Sec.1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date...you
-- will supply us with written confirmation...of a wellness visit...
-- occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary of the effective
-- date." Two sub-deadlines: the visit itself (<= 6 months) and the
-- supply of written confirmation of it (<= 7 months). Every benchmark
-- query that speaks to Sec.1.3 reports a single "confirmation
-- given/provided/submitted at N months" fact, with no separate figure
-- for the visit itself, so this encoding uses that one figure for both
-- sub-checks (recorded as a judgement call in NOTES.md).

`wellness visit deadline in months` MEANS 6
`wellness visit confirmation deadline in months` MEANS 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit occurred in time` claim MEANS
    claim's `months from effective date to wellness visit confirmation`
        AT MOST `wellness visit deadline in months`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit confirmation supplied in time` claim MEANS
    claim's `months from effective date to wellness visit confirmation`
        AT MOST `wellness visit confirmation deadline in months`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim MEANS
        `wellness visit occurred in time` claim
    AND `wellness visit confirmation supplied in time` claim

§§ `Sec.4.6 -- the one-year policy term`

`policy term in months` MEANS 12

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization occurred within the policy term` claim MEANS
    claim's `months from effective date to hospitalization`
        AT MOST `policy term in months`

§§ `Sec.1.2 -- deemed cancellation`

-- Cancelation is deemed to have occurred on: fraud/misrepresentation/
-- material withholding, OR the Sec.1.3 condition not being satisfied in
-- a timely fashion, OR the policy term having run out.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`
    OR  NOT (`condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim)
    OR  NOT (`hospitalization occurred within the policy term` claim)

§§ `Sec.1.1 -- is the policy in effect?`

-- Sec.1.1(1) the agreement is signed, and Sec.1.1(2) the premium has
-- been paid, are both assumed TRUE per the encoding brief and are not
-- modelled as Claim fields. Sec.1.1(3)'s "still pending" branch is not
-- separately modelled either: every claim in this benchmark supplies a
-- concrete wellness-visit-confirmation time, so "condition 1.3 satisfied
-- in a timely fashion" is always the operative branch, never "pending".

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect` claim MEANS
        `condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim
    AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)


§ `Benefits (Sec.2)`

`daily hospital income benefit amount` MEANS 500
`maximum benefit days` MEANS 365

-- Sec.2.3 -- "a claim must be made to the Company setting out the basis
-- for making the claim and for there being no exclusion or
-- cancellation." Evaluating `covered` below on a claim already
-- presupposes that a claim has been made; no separate Claim field
-- represents this procedural step.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization caused by a covered accidental injury` claim MEANS
        claim's `hospitalization caused by accidental injury`
    AND NOT (claim's `injury was self-inflicted`)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insured event occurred` claim MEANS
        claim's `hospitalization caused by sickness`
    OR  `hospitalization caused by a covered accidental injury` claim


§ `General exclusions (Sec.3)`

`age exclusion threshold` MEANS 80

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded cause of hospitalization` claim MEANS
        claim's `hospitalization arose out of skydiving`
    OR  claim's `hospitalization arose out of service in the military`
    OR  claim's `hospitalization arose out of service as a fire fighter`
    OR  claim's `hospitalization arose out of service in the police`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST `age exclusion threshold`


§ `General conditions (Sec.4)`

-- Sec.4.1 -- the policy insures the claimant twenty-four hours a day,
-- anywhere in the world; there is accordingly no territorial exclusion
-- to encode.
-- Sec.4.2 -- arbitration is a dispute-resolution mechanic, not a
-- coverage gate.
-- Sec.4.3 -- governing law (New York) does not affect whether a claim
-- is covered.
-- Sec.4.4 -- currency of payment does not affect coverage.
-- Sec.4.5 -- the premium is assumed already paid in one lump sum (see
-- Sec.1.1(2) above).
-- None of Sec.4.1-Sec.4.5 needs a Claim field or a predicate.


§ `Master rule -- does the policy cover this claim?`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered` claim MEANS
        `policy in effect` claim
    AND `insured event occurred` claim
    AND NOT (`excluded cause of hospitalization` claim)
